# Audit lanes

`AGENTS.md` is canonical. The house audit loop is three lanes over the full fix
diff: **code**, **security**, and **architect**. Gate: **0 CRITICAL, 0 HIGH,
0 MEDIUM**. LOW/INFO may carry explicitly.

In Codex sessions, use native Codex subagents/auditor lanes. Use OMC only as a
legacy fallback outside Codex contexts that lack native subagents:

```bash
omc ask codex --agent-prompt code-reviewer --prompt "<lane prompt>"
omc ask codex --agent-prompt security-reviewer --prompt "<lane prompt>"
omc ask codex --agent-prompt architect --prompt "<lane prompt>"
```

Run from the session/worktree root. Review the complete fix as it will land,
not an incremental follow-up slice.
